<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Untitled Document</title>
    <style>
        @import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Georgia:wght@400;600&amp;family=Times+New+Roman:wght@400;600&amp;display=swap');

        body {
            font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif;
            max-width: 800px;
            margin: 0 auto;
            padding: 40px 50px;
            background: #ffffff;
            color: #000000;
            line-height: 1.6;
            font-size: 14pt;
            box-shadow: 0 0 20px rgba(0,0,0,0.1);
        }

        .header {
            text-align: center;
            margin-bottom: 30px;
            border-bottom: 3px double #000;
            padding-bottom: 15px;
        }

        h1 {
            font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
            font-size: 18pt;
            margin: 0 0 8px 0;
            font-weight: 600;
        }

        .subtitle {
            font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
            font-size: 14pt;
            margin: 0;
            font-weight: normal;
            letter-spacing: 1px;
        }

        .section {
            margin: 25px 0;
            padding: 10px 0;
        }

        .section-title {
            font-family: 'Georgia', serif;
            font-size: 13pt;
            font-weight: 600;
            text-transform: uppercase;
            letter-spacing: 2px;
            margin-bottom: 12px;
            border-left: 4px solid #000;
            padding-left: 8px;
        }

        p {
            margin: 0 0 12px 0;
            text-align: justify;
        }

        .centered {
            text-align: center;
            margin: 15px 0;
        }

        .list {
            margin: 0 0 15px 0;
            padding-left: 20px;
        }

        .list li {
            margin: 6px 0;
        }

        .placeholder {
            width: 100%;
            height: 180px;
            background: #f0f0f0;
            border: 2px dashed #999;
            margin: 20px 0;
            display: flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            font-style: italic;
            color: #666;
            position: relative;
        }

        .placeholder::before {
            content: "Diagram / Image Area";
            font-size: 12pt;
        }

        .signature {
            width: 180px;
            height: 60px;
            margin: 40px 0 10px 0;
            border: 1px solid #000;
            display: inline-block;
            position: relative;
        }

        .signature::after {
            content: "Signature";
            position: absolute;
            bottom: 12px;
            left: 50%;
            transform: translateX(-50%);
            font-size: 10pt;
            color: #666;
        }

        .footer {
            margin-top: 60px;
            text-align: center;
            font-size: 10pt;
            border-top: 1px solid #999;
            padding-top: 15px;
        }

        /* Column simulation for multi-column feel */
        @media print {
            body { max-width: 100%; padding: 30px; }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div class="header">
        <h1>OFFICIAL TRANSCRIPT</h1>
        <div class="subtitle">NATIONAL HEALTH CONFERENCE • 2025</div>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <div class="section-title">Date &amp; Location</div>
        <p><strong>Monday, September 15, 2025</strong><br>
        Grand Ballroom, Hyatt Regency Convention Center<br>
        Chicago, Illinois</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <div class="section-title">Panelists</div>
        <p><strong>Dr. Elena Vargas</strong> – Lead Epidemiologist, CDC<br>
        <strong>Dr. Marcus Chen</strong> – Cardiologist, Johns Hopkins<br>
        <strong>Dr. Priya Sharma</strong> – Public Health Researcher, WHO</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <div class="section-title">Opening Remarks</div>
        <p>Good morning, distinguished attendees. Today we convene to address the rising incidence of cardiovascular complications linked to prolonged screen time. The statistics are alarming: over 68% of American adults spend more than eight hours daily on digital devices.</p>

        <p><strong>Key Fact:</strong> A recent study found that individuals averaging six or more hours of screen exposure per day show a 32% higher risk of developing hypertension compared to those under four hours.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <div class="section-title">Main Presentation</div>
        <p>Our first speaker will present the latest longitudinal data from the National Cardiovascular Health Survey.</p>

        <div class="centered">
            <div class="placeholder">[Graph: Screen time hours vs. Blood pressure levels – bar chart showing 32% risk increase]</div>
        </div>

        <p>Dr. Vargas will now walk us through the mechanisms.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <div class="section-title">Q&amp;A Session</div>
        <ul class="list">
            <li>What are the long-term effects of intermittent fasting on cardiovascular health?</li>
            <li>How effective are wearable devices in reducing sedentary behavior?</li>
            <li>Should schools implement mandatory screen-time limits?</li>
        </ul>

        <p><em>Panel discussion will follow after the break.</em></p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <div class="section-title">Conclusions &amp; Recommendations</div>
        <p>1. Implement daily screen-time caps of no more than four hours for adults.<br>
        2. Promote 10-minute movement breaks every hour.<br>
        3. Expand public awareness campaigns through digital and traditional media.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
        <div class="section-title">Closing Statement</div>
        <p><em>“Prevention is not just better than cure — it is the only cure.”</em><br>
        – Dr. Priya Sharma</p>
    </div>

    <div class="centered">
        <div class="signature"></div>
        <p style="margin-top: 8px; font-style: italic; font-size: 11pt;">Signature of Conference Chair</p>
    </div>

    <div class="footer">
        <p>© 2025 National Health Conference • Chicago, Illinois</p>
        <p style="margin-top: 10px;">This document is for archival and educational purposes only.</p>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
